Fixes pages cached in Varnish without X-Magento-Tags, which no purge can remove (magento/magento2#40281, upstream PR magento/magento2#41038).

Root cause: with a two-level cache and use_stale_cache enabled, RemoteSynchronizedCache::load() returns stale local data when the remote entry is gone and another process holds the regeneration lock. RuntimeStaleCacheStateModifier then disables full_page for the rest of the request. LayoutPlugin::afterGenerateElements() has already set public Cache-Control headers by then, but afterGetOutput() skips X-Magento-Tags because full page cache is no longer enabled. Varnish stores the page for the full TTL and no ban, including a full flush or a flush by URL, matches it; only a Varnish restart or the TTL removes it.
Fix: when the layout is cacheable but full page cache is disabled in afterGetOutput(), replace Magento public cache headers (detected the same way as Kernel::process(): public with s-maxage) with no-cache headers.

Gotcha: detection is limited to the public + s-maxage shape set by setPublicHeaders(), so intentionally private or no-cache responses stay untouched.

